        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ballstonspa.gov/321/Brief-History-of-Ballston-Spa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Village Hotel, built 1804‑1847, once served as a temperance house before becoming the Saratoga County Historical Society.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ballston.org/about-ballston-spa/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The West Mill Complex, once the largest chocolate factory in Saratoga County, still smells of chocolate today after a recent renovation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ballston.org/about-ballston-spa/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Ballston Spa National Bank, founded in 1838, remains one of the oldest continuously operating American banks.",
